UID: UC-READ-THE-CANON-APART-FROM-THE-WHITEBOARD
TITLE: With the whiteboard switched off, the page shows the claims, their edges, their ladders and the node index, as v1 did
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The operator switches the whiteboard system off. Every narrative, every Cites and Contains edge and every row backlink disappears; what remains is the canon's claims with the type grid, the ladders with live counts, the edges figure over the selection and the node index -- the shape of v1's canon-only screens. Switching work on adds WORK and its Crosses and Produces edges to the same figure.
<<<
